invariant: INV-11
file: quic.c
catches: srv_quic_both_test
builds: bin/srv_quic_both_test
reason: a ROLE=both object gives every QUIC session the server's Initial
  labels, because the build defines CH_ROLE_SERVER, so a session from
  ch_quic_init seals under "server in" and opens under "client in", the
  reverse of RFC 9001 section 5.2. A one-role object never shows it, and
  neither does a client and a server in two processes; colibri found it
  running both in one. The ROLE=both build of bin/srv_quic_test opens each
  session's Initial packet with the other.

--- old
#define CH_QUIC_SELF(q) ((q)->endpoint)
--- new
#define CH_QUIC_SELF(q) CH_QUIC_ENDPOINT_SERVER
